---
import TrainingLayout from "../../layouts/TrainingLayout.astro";
import Snippet from "../../components/training/Snippet.astro";
import Figure from "../../components/training/Figure.astro";
import ApiLink from "../../components/training/ApiLink.astro";
import ChapterLink from "../../components/training/ChapterLink.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/training/Callout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---
<TrainingLayout slug="vue">

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <Code lang="bash" frame="terminal" code="npm i @guiexpert/table @guiexpert/vue3-table" />
  <Snippet file="examples/vue/main.ts" title="frameworks/vue/src/main.ts" />

  <h2 id="component">The component</h2>
  <Snippet file="examples/vue/App.vue" title="frameworks/vue/src/App.vue" />
  <Figure src="fw-vue" caption="Vue 3: the same 100,000 orders. Click a cell – the header shows row and column." />

  <h2 id="rules">Rules for Vue</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Model and options are plain objects</strong> – no <code>ref()</code> or <code>reactive()</code> needed. The table
      keeps its own state; making 100,000 rows reactive would only cost memory.</li>
    <li>Events are Vue events: <code>@tableReady</code>, <code>@mouseClicked</code>, <code>@selectionChanged</code>,
      <code>@contextmenu</code> … The payload is the argument (<ApiLink name="TableApi" />, <ApiLink name="GeMouseEvent" /> …).</li>
    <li><code>mouseClicked</code> is debounced by <code>debounceMouseClickDelay</code> (default 150 ms), so a double click does not
      also report two single clicks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="plugin">Register globally</h3>
  <p>Instead of importing the component in every file, install the plugin (default export):</p>
  <Code lang="ts" title="main.ts" code={`import GuiexpertTablePlugin from "@guiexpert/vue3-table";

createApp(App).use(GuiexpertTablePlugin).mount("#app");`} />

  <Callout type="note" title="Options with defaults">
    <p>Always start options with <code>{"{ ...new TableOptions() }"}</code> and change only what you need – details in
      <ChapterLink slug="table-options" />.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="next">Next</h2>
  <p><ChapterLink slug="angular" /> – one source, nine Angular versions.</p>
</TrainingLayout>
